Subject: [PATCH BlueZ 0/4] mesh-tester: mesh advertising lifecycle tests

Tests for the kernel series "[PATCH 0/5] Bluetooth: MGMT: stop and
account mesh transmissions correctly", posted separately.

Patch 1 lets a test hook the client controllers of the emulator, which
the receiver cases use to count the advertising reports a scanning
client gets. Patch 2 fixes a leak in src/shared/mgmt.c that
LeakSanitizer reports for every mesh-tester run (an event handler
unregistered from inside its callback is never freed); it is
independent of the rest. Patch 3 enables fault injection in the tester
kernel config, which the rejected-start cases need; without it they are
reported as not run. Patch 4 adds the cases.

On bluetooth/master 08e90633377f with the kernel series (and the
posted mesh_tx cleanup it assumes) all 55 mesh-tester cases pass under
KVM and the 50 Send cases under TCG and valgrind; on the unpatched
kernel 18 of 55 pass. Without the cleanup the two rejected-start cases
fail. The receiver cases print the counts they see and only require one
packet, so they pass whichever way the kernel's Count deadline is
decided.

Iaroslav Voitovych (4):
  emulator/hciemu: Add hooks on client controllers
  shared/mgmt: Fix leak when unregistering from a notify callback
  doc: Enable fault injection in the tester kernel config
